      Blend mode - It controls how an element's colors blend with the colors of the background or elements behind it.
        Common values:
multiply — creates a darker blended effect.
screen — creates a lighter blended effect.
overlay — combines light and dark contrast.
difference — creates contrasting colors.
      Clip image - It lets you cut an image into a particular shape, such as a circle, triangle, or polygon.
      Psuedo effect - CSS has two related features that help you style elements without adding extra HTML.
A. Pseudo-classes (:)
They style an element when it is in a particular state.
Examples:
:hover — pointer is over an element.
:focus — element has focus.
:active — element is being activated.
:first-child — element is the first child.
B. Pseudo-elements (::)
They style a specific part of an element or insert decorative content.
Examples:
::before — inserts content before an element's content.
::after — inserts content after its content.
::first-letter — styles the first letter.
::first-line — styles the first line.
//C++ Operator Overloading
  
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
class Base{
    private:
    int a;
    public:
    void read(int x){
            a=x;
    }
    void display(void){
        cout<<"value of a is: "<<a;
        
    }
    void operator!(void)
    {
        a=!a;
    }   
};



    int main(){
        Base obj;
        obj.read(10);
        cout<<"Before calling Operator Overloading";
        obj.display();
        cout<<endl;
        !obj;
        cout<<"After calling Operator Overloading";
        obj.display();
        cout<<endl;
        return 0;
}
//OUTPUT
Before calling Operator Overloadingvalue of a is: 10
After calling Operator Overloadingvalue of a is: 0


    
      
